  "summary": "New conditioning schemes span pharmacophores, pockets, conjugate components and single-residue edits, while PBPK re-scoring changes which generated candidates rank well.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is constraint-conditioned generation across chemical and protein modalities. PharmaDiff conditions 3D diffusion on pharmacophores for ligand-based design; PFM uses a perturbed conditional probability path for pocket-conditioned flow matching, reporting Vina -7.12 on CrossDocked; CupOFMoCA enforces cross-component chemical constraints in discrete flows for PROTAC and peptide-drug conjugate assembly. On the protein side, Pallatom2 jointly models sequence, backbone, side chains and target contacts atom-to-atom with 65.9M parameters and reports experimental results, PAMP projects a differentiable turnover objective onto single-amino-acid substitutions, and PDZ-binding motifs are designed via directions in a shared affinity latent space. Evaluation is the shifting axis: PBPK simulations re-score PARP1 generated molecules so dose-driven exposure and safety limits reorder candidate rankings, while SF-GA redesigns predicted P-gp substrates under synthetic accessibility constraints. Supporting predictors (DTBNet, peptide toxicity models) supply the scoring functions such pipelines depend on.",
